let __v_2959 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"happy\",\"Glad, cheerful, pleased, content, delighted. Glad is the everyday one, content means quietly satisfied, and delighted is a big thing.\"],[\"sad\",\"Unhappy, down, miserable, low, gutted. Down and low are for a flat week, miserable and gutted for something that has actually happened.\"],[\"big\",\"Large, huge, enormous, vast, sizeable. Large is neutral and fits writing; huge and enormous are the spoken ones, and vast is for space rather than a thing.\"],[\"small\",\"Little, tiny, slight, compact, minor. Tiny is smaller than little, and minor is for importance rather than size.\"],[\"good\",\"Fine, solid, strong, decent, excellent. Fine is faint praise, decent is a real compliment in speech, and excellent is for something you would single out.\"],[\"bad\",\"Poor, weak, awful, dreadful, rubbish. Poor and weak are the calm written ones; awful and rubbish are how people say it out loud.\"],[\"said\",\"Said, asked, replied, muttered, shouted, whispered. Said is invisible and usually the right word - save the others for the two or three places where how it was said matters.\"],[\"nice\",\"Kind, friendly, thoughtful, pleasant, lovely. Kind and thoughtful are about what someone did; pleasant and lovely are about how something felt.\"],[\"tired\",\"Weary, worn out, exhausted, drained, sleepy. Sleepy means ready for bed, exhausted means past it, and drained is the one after a hard week.\"],[\"angry\",\"Cross, annoyed, furious, irritated, livid. Cross is the mild everyday word, annoyed and irritated are about a thing, and furious and livid are the top end.\"],[\"scared\",\"Frightened, afraid, nervous, anxious, terrified. Nervous is before, frightened is now, and terrified is the extreme of either.\"],[\"beautiful\",\"Lovely, stunning, gorgeous, striking, handsome. Beautiful is the safe one, stunning is a reaction, and handsome works for a building as well as a face.\"],[\"interesting\",\"Intriguing, absorbing, fascinating, notable, worth a look. Absorbing means it held your attention, fascinating is stronger, and notable is the neutral written one.\"],[\"important\",\"Key, vital, crucial, significant, essential. Significant is the calm report word; crucial and essential mean it cannot be left out.\"],[\"difficult\",\"Hard, tricky, demanding, awkward, challenging. Tricky is a puzzle, demanding is effort, and awkward is a person or a corner rather than a task.\"],[\"easy\",\"Simple, straightforward, effortless, quick, painless. Simple is about the steps, straightforward is about the instructions, and effortless is how it felt.\"],[\"funny\",\"Amusing, comical, hilarious, witty, odd. Witty is clever, hilarious is loud, and odd is the other meaning of funny.\"],[\"hungry\",\"Starving, peckish, famished, ravenous. Peckish is a bit, starving is an exaggeration everyone uses, and ravenous is the real thing.\"],[\"thank you\",\"Thanks, many thanks, thank you so much, I really appreciate it, much appreciated. Thanks is fine in a message and the longer ones belong in a card or after a real favour.\"],[\"sorry\",\"I apologise, my apologies, I'm sorry about that, excuse me. I apologise is the written one for a mistake, and sorry is warmer when you mean it.\"],[\"no\",\"Not this time, I can't, I'd rather not, that doesn't work for me. I'd rather not is the kindest firm one, and adding a reason of one clause is plenty.\"],[\"good luck\",\"Best of luck, all the best, fingers crossed, break a leg. Fingers crossed is the friendly one, and break a leg is only for performers.\"],[\"congratulations\",\"Well done, nice one, many congratulations, thrilled for you. Well done is for effort, congratulations for the news itself.\"],[\"delicious\",\"Tasty, mouthwatering, lovely, moreish, scrumptious. Tasty is the everyday one, mouthwatering is for how it looks, and moreish means you want more of it.\"],[\"clever\",\"Bright, sharp, smart, inventive, quick. Bright and smart are the everyday ones, sharp is fast on the uptake, and inventive is about ideas.\"],[\"brave\",\"Courageous, bold, gutsy, plucky, fearless. Courageous is the formal one, bold is about a decision, and gutsy is doing it while scared.\"],[\"busy\",\"Flat out, rushed, swamped, hectic, tied up. Flat out and swamped are the spoken ones, hectic is about the day, and tied up is the polite one.\"],[\"great\",\"Excellent, brilliant, superb, terrific, first-rate. Brilliant is the British spoken one, superb is the calm written one, and terrific is louder.\"],[\"quick\",\"Fast, swift, speedy, brisk, prompt. Fast is about speed, brisk is a pace you set, and prompt means on time.\"],[\"i dont know\",\"I'm not sure, I'm not certain, I couldn't say, I'd have to check. I'd have to check is the one that keeps you honest without sounding helpless.\"]]}")?;
